# Copy to mobile/.env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file must stay blank
# (CLAUDE.md hard constraint #4 — no secret, key or credential is ever committed).
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables reach the app: Expo inlines them into the bundle at
# build time. That also means anything here is readable by anyone holding the APK,
# so this file is for addresses, never for secrets. Every real credential
# (ORS key, LiveKit secret, Supabase JWT secret) lives server-side in the Go
# backend's environment — see backend/.env.example.

# Base URL of the Horizon Go backend. Unset -> http://10.0.2.2:8080 (Android
# emulator reaching the host machine). A physical phone needs a real address:
# a LAN IP for a bench test, or the deployed https:// URL for a road ride.
EXPO_PUBLIC_HORIZON_API_URL=

# Supabase project URL and anon (publishable) key (ADR-016). The anon key is
# deliberately NOT a secret — every Supabase client app ships it, it's meant to be
# public, and Row-Level Security is the actual security boundary, not key secrecy.
# This is not a violation of the "no secret ever committed" rule above: the real
# secret is SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET, which lives only in backend/.env and is never sent
# to the app. Don't "fix" this by moving the anon key server-side — it would just
# break the client for no security gain (ADR-016 §5).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
